// `P(x)`, `acc(P(x))` and `acc(P(x), write)` assert the same resource, so they
// are one wand structure. Silicon rejects this file (magic wand instance not
// found): its structure records whether an amount was written, so it tells
// `acc(Q(x), write)` and `Q(x)` apart although they denote the same wand. A
// deliberate, sound departure.
predicate P(x: Ref)
predicate Q(x: Ref)

method permission_spellings(x: Ref)
  requires P(x) && (acc(P(x)) --* acc(Q(x), write))
  ensures Q(x)
{ apply P(x) --* Q(x) }
